            <div xml:id="d568">

                <pb facs="0700" n="598" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg598"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10170/3–4.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Chargé to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexican Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-01-28"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 127.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Most Excellent Sir</hi>: Referring to the extradition
                    case of George Deering Reed, I have the honor to inform you, as you will please
                    see from the record of proceedings in the case which I send you under separate
                    cover, together with the requisite certificate of Judge Lanning, of the District
                    Court of New Jersey, that a favorable decision has been already given in the
                    case and an order issued that the offender may be delivered to the Mexican
                    authorities.</p>
                <p>By virtue thereof, I beg that, in the absence of any objection, you may be
                    pleased to issue the requisite warrant for the surrender of the offender.</p>
                <p>Accept anew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">José F. Godoy.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
